		<label>Norinco Type 88 LMG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 5.45x39mm. 30-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Norinco Type 88 is a select-fire rifle based on the Russian AK-74 but produced in China. Produced in the single digits in the 1980s, the rifles only appeared for exhibition at trade shows for a short time before filtering out into the civilian market. Unlike most other copies of the AK made in China, the military variant was only made for export - while the PLA did conduct trials with AK-74s for potential marine use, they were supplied from the USSR. Furthermore, it is unclear if there is any direct connection between the Chinese Type 88 and the North Korean Type 88, despite the designation and caliber.

This is a rare light machine gun (LMG) variant of the Type 88.</description>
